// Set scale directly from architectural scale
// The correct formula: PDF uses 72 points per inch
// At architectural scale, feetPerInch tells us how many real feet per paper inch
// So: 1 paper inch = feetPerInch real feet
//     72 PDF points = 1 paper inch = feetPerInch real feet
//     1 PDF point = feetPerInch/72 real feet
// When rendered at scale S: 1 PDF point = S pixels
// So: S pixels = feetPerInch/72 feet
//     pixels per foot = S * 72 / feetPerInch
